<Article
  title="The Aura Network: the big idea for later"
  description="Return to Aura. One beautiful room at a time."
  kicker="Later"
  date="2026-09-30"
>
  <p>Here is the long game. Down the road, Aura grow rooms will grow food for a free food network, and Thirst Contact units will bottle water from the sky for a free water network. Owners get paid to keep them running. It is a future expansion of the Aura network, and it is not open yet.</p>
  <RevealHeading as="h2">How it would work</RevealHeading>
  <p>You own the unit. You tend the garden or fill the bottles. The food and water go out free to the people who take them, and the network pays you for your part. Sponsors may put their name on a bottle or a harvest one day, and they will be ethical ones only.</p>
  <p>Not into it? No problem. Get a grow room and keep the salad. Get Thirst Contact and keep the water. The network is optional.</p>
  <RevealHeading as="h2">What it isn't</RevealHeading>
  <p>It is not a franchise, a territory for sale or a fee schedule, and there is nothing to sign up for on this site today. It is a plan, and we are telling you early.</p>
  <RevealHeading as="h2">Why say it now</RevealHeading>
  <p>Because it explains why we build the way we do. The rooms, the <a href="/farms">grow rooms</a> and <a href="/water">Thirst Contact</a> make more sense when you can see where they are headed. If you only want a room, the room is the whole deal. If the network sounds like you, join the waitlist and we will tell you when it opens.</p>
  <p>For now, the honest version is simple: the network is not live yet. The rooms come first.</p>
</Article>
